.TH "GH-PR.SH" "1" "November 2026" "arran4/dotfiles" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gh\-pr.sh \- interactive GitHub pull request creation helper
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBgh\-pr.sh\fR
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Prompt for a branch name, commit message, PR title and PR body; open the configured editor for the body; then, after confirmation, create a branch, stage all files with git add ., commit, push and open a PR using gh. It can optionally switch back to the original branch and merge or rebase locally.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBEDITOR\fR
Editor used to prepare the PR description (defaults to vim).
.SH NOTES
IMPORTANT: This helper stages all files, not only selected changes. Confirm the working tree is appropriate before using it.
.PP
The optional merge/rebase is a local Git operation, not a GitHub PR merge. Use this helper only when that workflow is intended.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
Run from a writable Git checkout with git and gh installed, authenticated
with permission to push branches and open pull requests. Configure the
repository using \fBgh repo set-default\fR. A terminal and EDITOR (or vim)
are required.
.SH INTERACTIVE WORKFLOW
The helper records the original branch, prompts for a branch name, commit
message and PR title, then opens an editor for the description. Lines
beginning with # are omitted. After confirmation it creates the new
branch, stages all files with git add ., commits, pushes to origin and
opens a PR. A failed push or PR creation does not roll back the earlier
steps.
.PP
The optional final merge or rebase affects local branches, not the
remote GitHub pull request.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
gh auth status
gh repo set-default
git status --short
gh-pr.sh
.fi
.SH TROUBLESHOOTING
If the repository check fails, run gh repo set-default in the checkout.
An EDITOR value must name a directly executable program. This helper is
interactive and has no noninteractive arguments. Inspect git status
before running: git add . may stage unrelated changes.
.SH SEE ALSO
gh(1), git(1)
